# Files never to upload in a CLI deploy (`vercel --prod`).
#
# Unlike a Git-triggered build, `vercel deploy` uploads the working directory
# and does NOT read .gitignore. Without this, local .env files ride along into
# the deployment — putting secrets in the build bundle and, worse, letting
# localhost values silently win for any variable not set in Vercel itself.
# That's how NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000 ends up baked into a
# production build, making every emailed quote link point at the recipient's
# own machine.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
node_modules
.next
.preview-emails
